WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
The Purdue Model matters because industrial operations depend on several kinds of systems

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.200
working together.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.000
Enterprise planning may create a production schedule.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Site operations translate that demand into work.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.090
Supervisory systems provide operator visibility, controllers execute logic,

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.000
and field instruments interact with the process.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.075
A failure or compromise can move through these dependencies even when the systems belong

00:00:20.075 --> 00:00:21.000
to different teams.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Placing functions into levels helps identify where connectivity should be limited.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.210
Traffic that stays within a control area has a different purpose from data being

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.000
transferred to enterprise analytics.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.930
The model supports segmentation by showing where trust changes and where controlled

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.985
intermediary services may be appropriate.

00:00:35.985 --> 00:00:38.200
It also supports risk analysis.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.000
Systems near the process may have direct safety and reliability consequences.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.020
Systems higher in the architecture may have broader user populations,

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.980
internet dependencies, and exposure to common enterprise threats.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:52.050
Neither is automatically more important; their risk comes from different functions,

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.000
pathways, and operational effects.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.215
The model improves communication between disciplines.

00:00:56.215 --> 00:01:00.250
Security teams can explain why direct enterprise-to-controller access creates risk.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.000
Engineers can explain why a control flow requires low latency or high availability.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Operators can identify which systems provide essential visibility.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.000
These conversations turn an abstract network diagram into an operational architecture.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.235
Finally, Purdue helps distinguish data flow from control flow.

00:01:15.235 --> 00:01:19.000
Production data may move upward for reporting, while commands, recipes,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.985
or configuration changes move downward under stricter authority.

00:01:21.985 --> 00:01:25.020
Reviewing both directions reveals remote access, update,

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.985
and administration paths that a simple data-flow discussion might miss.

00:01:27.985 --> 00:01:32.075
The goal is not to prevent communication, but to make every cross-level flow necessary,

00:01:32.075 --> 00:01:33.970
controlled, observable, and owned.
